ng  yeah it is complex so yesterday night  the taliban have like published  photos of their so-called special forces  going into the airport taking over  certain positions  this has apparently happened but as far  as i can tell this is like part of  the soon to to come hand over um so the  taliban haven't like  taken control of the whole airport just  off certain parts inside the airport  where they haven't been before  um and this seems to have been done in  coordination with the americans  okay france marty in kabul thanks so  much for your reporting  and for more on the group known as  islamic state khorasan or isk i'm joined  now by jan senpier  a counter-terrorism policy consultant  here in germany and thanks so much for  your time can you tell us how big of a  threat this group poses  well right now because of the  circumstances in kabul the the chaos the  opportunity for targets uh and and also  above all else the um the difficulties  in securing an area this group does  represent a high level of threat where  we're understanding better now how the  advantage to pull off the attack on  thursday and it really shows that they  they use the build vulnerabilities on  site uh to to carry out their attack and  the chaos just keeps growing therefore  they're still in a position to to be  extremely threatening  it doesn't you don't need high logistics  you know this is really a small scale  attack in terms of preparation  nonetheless it has big consequences and  therefore the logistics required uh  for such an attack  create the conditions where this group  can still be a highly threatening  describe to us what drives isk what are  they fighting for  well they're fighting for what they  consider to be the real islam the real  sharia and this really differentiates  them from from the taliban they consider  the taliban to be a group that moved  away from the real principles and values  of islam and for them that view is not  rigorous enough and this is what they're  pu